// ============================================================
// Brute Force Sign-in Detection (5 Minutes - Real-Time)
// ============================================================
// Purpose:    Detects rapid failed Entra ID sign-in attempts
//             from a single IP within a 5-minute window.
//             Designed for use in scheduled Sentinel analytic
//             rules for real-time alerting.
// MITRE:      T1110.001 - Brute Force: Password Guessing
// Lookback:   5 minutes
// Scheduled:  Every 5 minutes
// Severity:   Low (SSH Brute Force on Linux rule)
// Table:      SigninLogs (Entra ID)
// ============================================================

SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(5m)
| where ResultType != 0
| where isnotempty(IPAddress)
| summarize
    FailedAttempts  = count(),
    UsersTargeted   = make_set(UserPrincipalName)
    by IPAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 10m)
| where FailedAttempts >= 5
| order by FailedAttempts desc

// ============================================================
// Tuning Notes:
// - This query is the basis for the SSH Brute Force on Linux
//   and RDP Brute Force Attack analytic rules in Sentinel.
// - The bin(TimeGenerated, 10m) groups events into 10-minute
//   buckets for temporal analysis of attack patterns.
// - make_set(UserPrincipalName) shows all targeted accounts
//   from the same IP address in the same time window.
//
// When to use which version:
//   * 5-minute version: Use in Sentinel analytic rules
//     scheduled to run every 5-10 minutes for real-time alerts
//   * 1-hour version (brute-force-signin-1h.kql): Use in
//     hunting notebooks for broader retrospective analysis
//
// Lab Evidence:
//   This query powered the SSH Brute Force on Linux detection
//   rule which generated 2 confirmed alerts on linux-vm.
// ============================================================
